# ~/.ssh/config — managed by chezmoi (wsl-work only; ignored on other machines)

# Employer-specific hosts (corp git, VPN bastions) come from the private overlay.
# IMPORTANT: Include must precede all Host blocks. An Include placed *inside* a
# Host block is only processed when connecting to that host (ssh scopes it), which
# would hide config.d/* from every other host. First-match also means the overlay
# can override the cores below.
Include ~/.ssh/config.d/*

# Deploy key for the public dotfiles repo (read-only) — chezmoi update uses this.
# Source remote must be git@github-dotfiles:junior/dotfiles.git
# SSH over 443: the corp security stack (Azure-hosted egress — "connection closed by
# 4.208.x.x") intermittently kills outbound :22; ssh.github.com:443 is GitHub's
# official alternative endpoint (same host keys, same auth), and 443 egress is clean.
Host github-dotfiles
  HostName ssh.github.com
  Port 443
  User git
  IdentityFile ~/.ssh/dotfiles_deploy
  IdentitiesOnly yes

# Global defaults (catch-all; LAST so specific Host blocks and config.d/* win first-match).
# Keep long-running/idle sessions alive through corp NAT/firewall idle timeouts — the usual
# cause of "connection reset by peer" on the jump hosts: when the session goes quiet the
# middlebox drops its state, then RSTs the next packet. Encrypted SSH-layer keepalives keep
# traffic flowing so the state never expires. ServerAliveCountMax x ServerAliveInterval
# (~150s) is how long an actual network blip is tolerated before the client gives up;
# TCPKeepAlive no = rely on these forgiving SSH-layer probes, not the blunter TCP-layer ones.
Host *
  ServerAliveInterval 30
  ServerAliveCountMax 5
  TCPKeepAlive no
